WEBVTT

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.820
and then I close it ceremoniously.

00:06:30.844 --> 00:06:33.404
I literally move it so that
it kind of covers the desk

00:06:33.428 --> 00:06:35.236
just as a way to kind of switch off.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.292
AG: One of my favorite
insights about teams

00:06:37.316 --> 00:06:39.235
is that they're kind of like amplifiers:

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:41.546
whatever you put in comes out louder.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:43.946
When we go remote, that's even more true.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.768
All of our microphones
are blasting at once,

00:06:46.792 --> 00:06:48.556
and that can cause problems.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.668
MH: I sometimes think about it
as kind of like an iceberg, right?

00:06:51.692 --> 00:06:54.760
At the top of the iceberg,
the stuff that's more obvious --

00:06:54.784 --> 00:06:57.422
you know, it's just
difficult to communicate,

00:06:57.446 --> 00:07:00.116
partly because of the technology, right?